<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CSP> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, sandy, peaty [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CSPV> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, sandy, peaty, gravelly [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CSPZ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, sandy, peaty, silty [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CSPZV> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, sandy, peaty, silty, gravelly [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CSSST> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Silicate-sandstone, coarse"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CSST> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Sandstone, carbonaceous"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CST> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Claystone - A type of mudstone. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/03, fig. 13. See: silicate-claystone."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CSV> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, sandy, gravelly [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
