<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CSZVLB> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, sandy, silty, gravelly, cobbly, bouldery [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CSZVP> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, sandy, silty, gravelly, peaty [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CUR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Cumulate-rock - A type of rock of restricted mineralogy. Cumulate is a term used for igneous rocks formed by crystal settling in a magma chamber, i.e. it is a genetic term. Some of the physical processes involved in producing cumulates result in sub-monomineralic layers. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 8.2."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CV> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, gravelly [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CVB> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, gravelly, bouldery [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CVBS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, gravelly, bouldery, sandy [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CVBSZ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, gravelly, bouldery, sandy, silty [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/CVBZ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, gravelly, bouldery, silty [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme]"@en .
