<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/GMGN> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Microgranite, granophyric"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/GN> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granite - A type of granitic-rock. In the Rock Classification Scheme, it is a coarse-grained crystalline igneous rock whose mineral mode plots in field 3 of the quartz - alkali feldspar - plagioclase - feldspathoid (QAPF) diagram. Granite may be subdivided into syenogranite and monzogranite. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.1 and figs. 9, 11, 12."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockName/GNAK> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granite, alkali"@en .
